  "description": "Original constructed exercises bridging mathematically prepared students into graduate macroeconomic core models. Prerequisites: intermediate microeconomics and macroeconomics, multivariable calculus, constrained optimization, probability and conditional expectations, difference equations, and basic eigenvalue analysis. Continuous-time exercises also require elementary differential equations. All numerical scenarios are hypothetical; official course materials guide coverage, not copied questions or empirical claims.",
